## Why This Is Asked

Tests ownership, bias-for-action, and customer-obsession under production risk. It requires concrete triage steps, defined metrics, and clear decision criteria that tie business impact to user experience.

## Key Concepts

- Ownership and incident command
- Real-time metrics and fairness indicators
- Customer impact and transparent communication
- Predefined decision thresholds and post-incident process

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode for rapid rollback decision threshold
function decideRolloutDisaster(metrics, thresholds) {
  if (metrics.groupDisparity > thresholds.disparity) return 'rollback';
  if (metrics.loss > thresholds.loss) return 'patch';
  return 'slow-roll';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the patch without regressing fairness?
- What monitoring dashboards would you add post-rollback?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes real-time risk handling, cross-functional negotiation, and release engineering under regulatory pressure.

## Key Concepts

- Incident risk assessment and decision framing
- Canary releases and feature flags
- Rollback plans and rollback testing
- Privacy, regulatory compliance, and data governance
- Stakeholder alignment and concise communication

## Code Example

```javascript
// gated rollout example
if (featureFlags.analyticsEnabled && privacy.isCompliant()) {
  enableAnalytics();
} else {
  enableFallbackAnalytics();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure success of the chosen path?
- What changes would you make to incident playbooks to cover similar risks in the future?
